  "historical_output_text": " Be sure to provide any safety tips and materials needed.\nTask: Cleaning the lint filter in a clothes dryer\n\nPreparation:\n1. Turn off the dryer and unplug it from the wall outlet. \n2. Locate the lint filter, usually on the front of the dryer. \n3. Remove any clothing or debris from around the dryer.\n4. If necessary, remove the lint filter cover or door to access the lint filter.\n\nMain steps:\n1. Pull out the lint filter from the dryer. \n2. Remove any lint, hair, or other debris from the filter.\n3. Rinse the lint filter in the sink with water to remove any remaining debris. \n4. If using a washable mesh lint filter, you can also wash it in a dishwasher on the air-dry cycle.\n5. Allow the lint filter to air dry",
